We have derived improved differentiability properties for solutions to a non-autonomous obstacle problem, formulated as
  \begin{equation*}
  \min \left\{\int_{\Omega}f\left(x, Dv(x)\right)dx\,:\, v\in
  \mathcal{K}_\psi(\Omega)\right\},
  \end{equation*}
  where the function $f$ exhibits only partial convexity with respect to the gradient. Under the assumption of partial, 1-homogeneous convexity, we have obtained a result on higher differentiability for data and obstacles belonging to a specific range of Sobolev spaces. Furthermore, we have achieved an understanding of partial regularity for data and obstacles in a broader range of Sobolev spaces, where the resulting differentiability is $\max\{2,p-1\}$. Our approach has been made possible by a novel technical finding, which we have also utilized to prove an internal growth condition in a specific set domain.
